{
 "name": "wrap-up-statuses",
 "comment": "Superior wrap-up statuses, in-review, and dropped. ada leads maya (who leads lena) and raj; bo is a second root. 1: raj (a peer) assigns lena; ada, her indirect superior, sets done: final, no review, and raj gets a done notice. 2: maya blocks lena's assignment, lena leaves it with doing; ada blocks it, then drops it: the item shows dropped. 3: maya closes under completion assigner: in-review, ada confirms. 4: lena closes bo's ask; maya (her superior, not the assigner) rejects it to doing. 5: lena's close of bo's second ask waits in bo's confirm list. 6: lena puts her self-assigned task in review and confirms it as its assigner; another she leaves with doing; raj enters in-review voluntarily on ada's ask (ada's confirm list). 7: on Mixed maya closes and raj drops: the item is done; raj drops and reopens Reopened: doing. 8: Parent's dropped child stays out of its roll-up, the done child counts; ada gets a dropped notice. 9: an assign without completion keeps the assignee default, so maya's close is done. 10: maya's done and lena's doing are concurrent; one register, the later write shown. 11: maya blocks the fallback record of lena's own task.",
